    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "For q-332550, substituting y_p=ax^2+bx+c gives a=-1, 2a+b=2 and b+c=-3, hence y_p=-x^2+4x-7. Adding Ae^{-x} gives the general solution; differentiation verifies y'+y=-x^2+2x-3. For q-33662, P corresponds to t=1. The derivative is r'(t)=⟨1,8/t,4t⟩, so r'(1)=⟨1,8,4⟩ has magnitude sqrt(1+64+16)=9. Normalization gives ⟨1/9,8/9,4/9⟩. Both answers agree with their respective captured Math Academy worked solutions.",
